 {title:"Tension Architecture",phase:"MUSICAL NARRATIVE",pages:"78–97",level:"Unknown",concept:"Advanced improvisation is not the number of outside notes. It is the shape of tension across time.",why:"Listeners follow density, register, rhythm, repetition and harmonic distance as a story. A climax works when earlier phrases prepare it and the return releases accumulated pressure.",failure:"Starting at maximum intensity, staying outside without development, or resolving harmonically while rhythm and register remain chaotic.",setup:"Evolving 32-bar form · 90 BPM · record one uninterrupted take",task:"Draw an eight-point tension curve. Assign home, colour, approach, side-slip and release devices before playing.",apply:"Perform low → develop → disrupt → climax → release. Leave at least 25% silence and reuse one motif in every section.",pass:"Recorded tension follows the planned curve; climax is unique; final eight bars re-establish home; explain three decisive moments.",target:0,out:1}
